<title>LATVIA: Latvia, IMF reach new standby agreement-finmin.</title>
<headline>Latvia, IMF reach new standby agreement-finmin.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvian Finance Minister Robert Zile said on Tuesday that his government had reached a new standby loan agreement with the International Monetary Fund (IMF).</p>
<p>&quot;We have agreed on a new memorandum for 18 months until March 1999. The official signing could take place in September,&quot; Zile told a news conference. No details of the size of the standby agreement were given.</p>
</text>
